"""Original network and communications security scenarios."""
ITEMS=[]
def group(o,rows):
 for k,(s,e) in enumerate(rows):ITEMS.append((s,[o[k]]+[v for j,v in enumerate(o) if j!=k],e))
group(['A network-layer routing decision','A transport-layer port check','An application-layer request check','A link-layer forwarding decision'],[
('A device chooses the next hop toward a destination IP subnet. Which type of decision is being made?', 'Routing toward an IP destination is a network-layer function.'),
('A rule permits TCP destination port 443 while denying TCP destination port 23. Which type of check is this?', 'TCP ports are transport-layer identifiers. A port number alone does not prove the application content is safe.'),
('A gateway examines the structure of an HTTP request before deciding whether to allow it. Which type of check is this?', 'HTTP request semantics are application-layer information rather than merely a port or IP route.'),
('Within an Ethernet segment, a switch uses a destination MAC address to select a forwarding interface. Which type of decision is this?', 'MAC-based Ethernet forwarding is a link-layer function.')])
group(['A stateful firewall','A web application firewall','A network intrusion detector','A network access control service'],[
('A perimeter device tracks established connection state and uses it when evaluating return traffic. Which control is described?', 'A stateful firewall evaluates traffic in the context of tracked connections.'),
('A team needs a control focused on suspicious HTTP request patterns directed at a public web application. Which control is designed for that role?', 'A web application firewall focuses on web application traffic. It supplements rather than replaces secure application code.'),
('A sensor receives mirrored traffic and generates alerts, but is not in the forwarding path and cannot directly drop those packets. Which control is described?', 'A passive network intrusion detector observes and alerts without acting as an inline packet-blocking control.'),
('A joining endpoint is evaluated against device and identity policy before receiving the appropriate network access. Which control is described?', 'Network access control evaluates admission or placement according to the organization’s access policy.')])
group(['Separate the guest network','Restrict inter-segment traffic','Protect the management interface','Place the sensor on the required path'],[
('Visitor laptops currently share the same unrestricted network as internal workstations. Which design change first establishes distinct access zones for those populations?', 'Separate the guest network into an appropriately controlled zone rather than treating visitors as internal peers.'),
('Two VLANs exist, but the router permits all traffic between them. Which change makes their security boundary enforce the intended permitted flows?', 'Enforce inter-segment policy at the routing or filtering boundary. VLAN separation alone does not guarantee traffic restrictions.'),
('A network appliance exposes its administrative service to all user subnets. Which change reduces the unnecessary administrative exposure?', 'Restrict and protect management access using approved administrative paths and authentication.'),
('A detection sensor monitors internet ingress, but the suspicious traffic moves only between internal server segments. Which placement change improves visibility for this case?', 'Observe the path carrying the relevant internal traffic; a sensor cannot inspect traffic that never reaches it.')])
group(['A site-to-site VPN','A remote-access VPN','A virtual desktop service','An application reverse proxy'],[
('Two office gateways maintain a protected tunnel carrying traffic between their private networks. Which access pattern is this?', 'A site-to-site VPN connects networks through their gateways.'),
('An employee’s managed laptop establishes an authenticated tunnel into the organization while away from the office. Which access pattern is this?', 'A remote-access VPN connects an individual remote endpoint to permitted organizational resources.'),
('A user interacts with a centrally hosted desktop session while applications and working data remain in that hosted environment. Which access pattern is this?', 'Virtual desktop access presents a remote desktop session; controls are still needed for permitted data transfers.'),
('External users reach one published web application through a gateway that forwards requests to its backend, without joining the internal network. Which access pattern is this?', 'A reverse proxy fronts the published application rather than granting general network membership.')])
group(['Verify the wireless authentication server','Use individual enterprise credentials','Isolate untrusted wireless clients','Retire unsupported wireless equipment'],[
('A managed Wi-Fi client must avoid accepting an impersonated enterprise authentication server during its configured EAP method. Which check addresses this risk?', 'Correct server-certificate validation helps prevent trusting an impersonated authentication service.'),
('An organization needs to revoke one employee’s Wi-Fi access without changing a shared secret for everyone. Which identity design supports that need?', 'Individual enterprise credentials allow per-user lifecycle and revocation rather than reliance on one shared passphrase.'),
('A public Wi-Fi service should prevent visitors from directly reaching other guests’ devices. Which network behavior should be configured?', 'Client isolation limits direct guest-to-guest reachability where supported and correctly configured.'),
('An access point cannot receive security fixes and cannot meet the organization’s required wireless protection. Which lifecycle response addresses the persistent limitation?', 'Replace or retire unsupported equipment under the approved plan rather than assume configuration can add unavailable capabilities.')])
group(['Distributed denial of service','On-path interception','DNS cache poisoning','Unauthorized network attachment'],[
('Many distributed sources overwhelm a public service so legitimate clients cannot obtain responses. Which threat pattern is described?', 'Distributed denial of service targets availability through traffic or resource exhaustion from multiple sources.'),
('An adversary is positioned between communicating endpoints and attempts to observe or alter their exchanges. Which threat pattern is described?', 'An on-path adversary can intercept traffic; authenticated protected channels help address this threat.'),
('A resolver stores a forged name-to-address result and subsequently directs users to the wrong destination. Which threat pattern is described?', 'DNS cache poisoning introduces false resolution data into a cache.'),
('An unapproved device connects to an office network port and obtains access intended only for managed endpoints. Which threat pattern is described?', 'The issue is unauthorized network attachment, which admission and port controls can help address.')])
group(['Upstream traffic filtering','Authenticated channel protection','DNSSEC validation','Network admission enforcement'],[
('A volumetric attack saturates the organization’s internet circuit before local equipment can process traffic. Which measure addresses the bottleneck at a useful location?', 'Upstream filtering or scrubbing can reduce attack traffic before it consumes the constrained link.'),
('A client communicates across an untrusted network and must detect peer impersonation and message modification. Which control directly protects the exchange?', 'An authenticated protected channel provides peer validation and integrity when configured correctly.'),
('A validating resolver must detect forged signed DNS data using a configured chain of trust. Which mechanism supplies this validation?', 'DNSSEC validates signed DNS data using trust relationships; it does not encrypt ordinary DNS queries.'),
('Only approved devices should obtain normal access through enterprise network ports. Which mechanism enforces that joining condition?', 'Network admission enforcement can evaluate identity and device policy before granting the permitted access.')])
group(['Limit the IoT device’s network paths','Validate the firmware update source','Replace default device credentials','Plan for the device’s end of support'],[
('A building sensor needs to report only to one management service but can currently contact every internal subnet. Which change reduces unnecessary reachability?', 'Restrict its network paths to the required communications and manage exceptions explicitly.'),
('A device administrator receives a firmware image through an unverified message. What must be established before installing it?', 'Verify the authorized source and integrity through the vendor’s supported validation process.'),
('A newly installed device still uses the manufacturer’s widely known initial login. Which provisioning action addresses this immediate credential weakness?', 'Replace default credentials and establish the approved identity configuration before normal operation.'),
('A vendor announces that security maintenance for a deployed sensor will end next year. Which lifecycle activity should begin?', 'Plan a supported replacement or approved retirement and manage exposure during the transition.')])
group(['Review the rule’s business owner','Check the rule order','Test the intended traffic flow','Remove the expired exception'],[
('A firewall exception remains active, but no team can explain its purpose or accept responsibility for it. Which governance information is missing?', 'An accountable owner and justified purpose are needed to review whether the exception remains appropriate.'),
('A specific deny rule never takes effect because an earlier broad allow rule matches first in a first-match policy. What must be examined?', 'Rule order determines which matching action is applied in a first-match policy.'),
('A proposed firewall change has been approved, but the team needs evidence that the required application still works and prohibited paths remain blocked. Which activity supplies that evidence?', 'Test representative permitted and denied flows rather than relying only on a syntactically valid configuration.'),
('A temporary partner connection was authorized only until a project ended yesterday, and no extension is approved. Which lifecycle action follows?', 'Remove or disable the expired exception through the authorized process so temporary access does not become permanent.')])
group(['Use authenticated, encrypted administrative access','Synchronize the device clock','Centralize device event collection','Back up the approved configuration'],[
('A router’s administration currently uses an unprotected remote session. Which management-plane improvement protects the administrator’s exchange?', 'Use approved authenticated encrypted administration, such as properly configured SSH, and restrict its reachability.'),
('Network device events cannot be accurately correlated because their timestamps differ substantially. Which operational control addresses this?', 'Maintain appropriate time synchronization and record time-zone information for useful correlation.'),
('A failed appliance may take its locally stored event history with it. Which logging design reduces dependence on that single local store?', 'Forward relevant events to a protected central collection service while managing delivery and retention.'),
('A replacement appliance must be rebuilt after hardware failure. Which maintained artifact helps restore the intended policy?', 'A protected backup of the approved configuration supports controlled reconstruction and validation.')])
assert len(ITEMS)==40
